Summary:

Removed the "Total Fees / Paid / Balance / Payment Status" summary grid from the Billing section in ParentPortal.tsx (the "Billing Summary" block just above Payment History). billingInfo is still used for the CSV export, so that logic is untouched.
Diagnosed the "Tuition Payment Breakdown shows 0" issue: it's a data gap, not a code bug. The tuition_fees table has zero rows for the currently-active 2026-2027 school year (starting a new school year doesn't carry forward tuition fee configs by design), so every "Tuition Fee" line item computes to 0 and gets filtered out, leaving the grid looking empty. You've chosen to configure those amounts yourself via Admin → System Settings → Tuition Management, so no data changes were made.




Parent Dashboard (Billing and Payment Section)
- I want the grid of the Tuition Payment Breakdown Grid to be dynamic to be able to reflect in real time. When I change the tuition fee of the Elementary level to 5,000 it still showed 2,400 on the new student that I just enrolled. The amount of the fees are subject for change at any point of time that's why I want the grids to be dynamic and catch informaton live.
- On the Main Dashboard the grid titled "Tuition Details" it must contain the Enrollment Fee. Fix also the remarks to the side of the amount not underneath the name. Also add the Enrollment fee to the Tuition Payment Breakdown as well

Summary:

Root-caused the stale ₱2,400 as an RLS gap, not a stale-cache/frontend bug: tuition_fees and enrollment_fees only had SELECT policies for staff roles (current_staff_role() IS NOT NULL), with no policy covering parents/guardians. So every Parent Portal query against those tables silently returned zero rows under RLS, and the code's `{...DEFAULT_TUITION_FEES, ...liveRows}` fallback quietly filled in with the hardcoded default (2400 for Elementary) — no matter what the Admin actually configured, and no amount of reloading the page would fix it. Added an "authenticated read" SELECT policy on both tables (auth.uid() IS NOT NULL), matching the existing school_years pattern, on the live SIMS_TESTING Supabase project — applied via migration `allow_authenticated_read_tuition_and_enrollment_fees` and verified in pg_policies.
The "Tuition Details" grid (Dashboard) and "Tuition Payment Breakdown" grid (Billing tab) already computed and displayed an Enrollment Fee line item in the existing (uncommitted) code — no change needed there.
Tuition Details remarks: moved the PAID/PARTIAL/UNPAID/APPLIED status badge from underneath the item label to sit beside the amount, in ParentPortal.tsx's per-child Tuition Details cards.
npx tsc --noEmit passes clean.